'''Important note:''' The μ_eff values above are for the ferrofluid alone. Within the TPMS composite, the ferrofluid fills only 3–5% of the total volume (dedicated microchannels). The effective composite μ_ψ is therefore much closer to μ₀ than the pure ferrofluid values suggest — the composite μ_ψ is dominated by the polymer matrix (μ_ψ ≈ μ₀). The coherence length control works through the spatial arrangement of the ferrofluid channels relative to the ψ field mode shape, not through bulk permeability modification of the entire composite.

The precise relationship between ferrofluid channel H-field, composite μ_ψ, and resulting L_ψ requires numerical computation (COMSOL magnetic + ψ field coupled solver) calibrated against TML-1 measurements. The table above gives the engineering set-points; the calibration data from TML-1 populates the [[Anchor Controller]] (D6) look-up table.

